WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Fluorine-18 is radioactive.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.010
Its nuclei emit positrons, with
a half-life of about 110 minutes.

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.630
A positron travels only a
tiny distance through tissue,

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.530
then meets an electron.

5
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.360
Matter meets antimatter,
and both annihilate.

6
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.190
All their mass becomes gamma radiation.

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.870
How can that tiny burst
help doctors find a tumour?

8
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.340
In this mission, you'll attach
fluorine-18 to a glucose-like molecule,

9
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:30.250
and follow where it collects.

10
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.410
Then you'll weigh a PET
scanner against a gamma camera:

11
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.210
cost, sharpness and availability.

12
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.540
Your mission: explain how this meeting
of matter and antimatter inside the body

13
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.390
helps doctors find a tumour.
